===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q39614}}A place where the [[dead]] are [[buried]]; a [[graveyard]] or [[memorial park]].
#* {{RQ:Mary Shelley Last Man|II|2|passage=The plain around was interspersed with '''cemeteries''', Turk, Greek, and Armenian, with their growth of cypress trees...}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year= 1970 |author=Kazimierz Godłowski|title=The chronology of the Late Roman and early migration periods in Central Europe|work=Acta scientiarum litterarumque: Schedae archeologicae|url= https://openlibrary.org/books/OL5346309M|publisher=Nakładem Uniwersytetu Jagiellonśkiego|page=22|text= They were probably the work of individual craftsmen working to meet the chieftains' needs. Their place in the chronology of the big '''cemeteries''' is indicated by the less richly-decorated double-springed bronze brooches which are found here.}}
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|page=26|passage={{...}} the '''cemetery''' – which people of shattering wit like Sampson never tired of calling ‘the [[dead centre]] of town’ {{...}}}}

